From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryson <10244083+brysonwf@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 09:55:42 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom_smbx: apply the programmed input current
 limit without APSD

When APSD never completes - a PC port while the USB controller is in device mode owns D+/D- - the programmed
USBIN current limit is ignored and the input stays at the default. Set ICL_OVERRIDE after writing the limit so the
value written through current_max takes effect.

This patch was written by Claude (Anthropic's AI assistant) under the direction of Bryson, who reviewed and
tested it on a Surface Duo.

Signed-off-by: Bryson <10244083+brysonwf@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c
index 0ab98fb16..fdc9e490d 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c
@@ -429,8 +429,13 @@ static int smb_set_current_limit(struct smb_chip *chip, unsigned int val)
 	}
 	val_raw = val / CURRENT_SCALE_FACTOR;
 
-	return regmap_write(chip->regmap, chip->base + USBIN_CURRENT_LIMIT_CFG,
-			    val_raw);
+	int rc = regmap_write(chip->regmap, chip->base + USBIN_CURRENT_LIMIT_CFG, val_raw);
+
+	/* use the programmed limit even when APSD never completes (PC port + USB gadget) */
+	if (!rc)
+		rc = regmap_update_bits(chip->regmap, chip->base + CMD_ICL_OVERRIDE,
+					ICL_OVERRIDE_BIT, ICL_OVERRIDE_BIT);
+	return rc;
 }
 
 static void smb_status_change_work(struct work_struct *work)
